 person would say.</li>\n<li>Talk about the things you both wrote and think about these questions:</li>\n<ul>\n<li>Which arguments were more effective. Why?</li>\n<li>Which arguments were less effective. Why?</li>\n<li>What kind of argument would be more likely to persuade the other side to change their mind? Why?</li>\n</ul>\n</ol>\n", "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": false, "selectedModalId": null, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": {"heading": "", "checkList": [{"key": "89MYpq0iyhXn3_tCo6O7U", "checked": false, "listItem": ""}], "description": ""}, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"id": 478526453, "text": null, "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 3, "btnType": "PRIMARY", "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "EDITOR", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{'headers':['Col1'],'rows':[{'col1':'row1'},{'col1':'row2'}, {'col1':'row3'}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 478521934, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": "<h2>First, thinking:</h2>\n<p>Each player must pick a side, either agreeing or disagreeing with the statement above.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Write down five things you could say to support your argument.</li>\n<li>Write down any things you think your opponent might say to support their argument.</li>\n<li>Looking at what you wrote for step 2, think of counter-arguments (ways to argue back against them).</li>\n</ol>\n", "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": false, "selectedModalId": null, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": {"heading": "", "checkList": [{"key": "h